  {
    q: "Is my wood-fired oven SCAQMD compliant?",
    a: "Depends on installation date and configuration. South Coast Air Quality Management District has rules on commercial wood-burning equipment in LA, OC, Riverside, San Bernardino. Pre-existing installs are typically grandfathered. New installs face stricter requirements. Some brands (Wood Stone Fire Deck) offer gas-assist versions for compliance, wood-fire taste with gas temperature control. We document your unit's compliance status and refer to SCAQMD compliance specialists if your operation faces a permit issue."
  },
  {
    q: "What's gas-assist on a wood-fired oven?",
    a: "Wood Stone Fire Deck and some Forno Bravo Professionale models offer gas-assist configurations. A gas burner inside or adjacent to the dome maintains base temperature, allowing the oven to start faster, recover faster between bakes, and operate during low-volume periods without lighting wood fire. The wood fire is added on top of the gas base for flavor. Compliance-friendly. We service the gas-assist component (burner, igniter, thermocouple) plus the standard refractory."
  },
  {
    q: "Do you service Forno Bravo, Wood Stone, Marra Forni, and Pavesi?",
    a: "Yes. These four brands cover the LA premium wood-fired market. Forno Bravo (independent California, modular dome, Casa series, Professionale 110 and Professionale 130), Wood Stone (independent Washington state, Mountain Series, Fire Deck gas-assist), Marra Forni (Italian premium, Rotator deck variants), Pavesi (Italian premium, Capri series). Most appliance shops decline wood-fired ovens. We do them."
  },
  {
    q: "Why don't most appliance shops service wood-fired ovens?",
    a: "Wood-fired oven service is a specialty trade. Limited mechanical components (mostly refractory dome plus floor stone plus damper plus thermometer plus optional gas-assist), specialty diagnostic, and SCAQMD compliance awareness required for LA-area commercial operations. Most general appliance shops don't have the brand familiarity or the refractory-contractor partnerships. We do."
  },
  {
    q: "What's typical service-call cost on a wood-fired oven?",
    a: "$120 commercial diagnostic, applied toward repair. Service-call mechanical repairs (gas-assist burner, igniter, damper actuator, thermometer) typically run $440 to $1,400. Refractory work (dome cracking, floor stone replacement) is a specialty referral, $1,800 to $4,800+ depending on scope. We diagnose, document, quote, refer if specialty work needed."
  },
  {
    q: "What's your warranty?",
    a: "90 days SDAR labor warranty on the work we perform directly. Refractory work performed by partner specialty contractors carries their own warranty. BHGS #A49573, EPA 608 Universal certified #1346255700410, BBB Accredited Business."
  },
  {
    q: "Why is my wood-fired pizza oven taking longer to heat up?",
    a: "On a gas-assist wood-fired oven (Wood Stone Fire Deck, some Forno Bravo Professionale models), slow dome warm-up almost always points to the gas-assist burner component. A gas burner inside or adjacent to the dome maintains base temperature so the oven starts and recovers faster; when its igniter or thermocouple fails, the dome relies on wood fire alone and warm-up stretches out. Replacing the igniter and thermocouple runs $440 to $980, and we verify gas-assist startup and steady-state operation before leaving. On a traditional wood-only dome with no gas assist, slow heat-up usually means a damper or airflow issue instead. Same Day Appliance Repair diagnoses it on a $120 commercial diagnostic, waived with repair."
  },
  {
    q: "Do I need an SCAQMD permit to repair my wood-fired pizza oven?",
    a: "Repairing existing equipment is different from installing or modifying it. The South Coast Air Quality Management District has rules on commercial wood-burning equipment in LA, Orange, Riverside, and San Bernardino counties; pre-existing installs are typically grandfathered, while new installs face stricter requirements. A straight repair of a grandfathered oven generally doesn't trigger a new permit, but we don't make that determination for you, we document your unit's configuration and compliance status and refer you to an SCAQMD compliance specialist if your operation faces a permit question. Our scope is the mechanical repair (gas-assist burner, damper, thermometer) plus refractory coordination, not SCAQMD permit application work, which is a separate environmental compliance trade."
  }
];

